From: edde746 <86283021+edde746@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/http: persistent range requests (backport)

n8.0.1 opens a connection for every seek: http_seek_internal() calls
http_open_cnx() on a fresh URLContext whatever multiple_requests says,
which only changes the Connection header. mpv's stream layer seeks while
it opens a file (to an index at the end of the file and back, then to
the resume position), so a Matroska or MP4 file with its index at the end
costs three or four TCP and TLS handshakes before the first frame.

Upstream has since taught the protocol to keep the connection: a reply
whose remaining bytes are within the short seek size is read out and the
next request goes over the same connection (a "soft seek"),
initial_request_size bounds the requests made while a file is opened so
that little is left to read out, request_size bounds every request, a
range that ends before the file does is continued with another request,
and multiple_requests became a tristate that keeps the connection alive
whenever a request is bounded. This is that work, for libavformat/http.c
only, as it stands on release/9.1 (and master) and with the fixes that
followed it there, in upstream order:

  5f95a1e714 fix noop seek check
  19cae9151c print error on HTTP response failure
  ca2c5ff412 parse range size from Content-Range header
  6336fa3335 return EIO if s->hd is NULL
  bf1722a9c6 request more data after partial response
  e03b034e45 re-use keep-alive connection for small seeks
  4f5d91e43f allow limiting initial request size
  b8daba42cd report connection statistics
  ba3639bc90 allow adjusting the redirect limit
  82fbb04d07 Also count redirects from the cache
  4cefbc54c4 add missing check to connection re-use
  2e7078cda6 add -request-size option
  fb7558dcb0 avoid int overflow
  f5ddf1c4a8 fix http_connect() offset mismatch error code
  142d999fda restore offset on http_open_cnx() failure
  fcc1a03a0e move retry label (cosmetic)
  7a348f662d close stale connection on wrong seek
  90dae166b5 Fix shadowing
  7cb93fb200 return ENOSYS instead of UINT64_MAX for unknown filesize
  8712114200 properly re-set s->range_end before requests
  557ab6f2ab make short-seek logic more robust
  62006041cc don't return EOF unless we actually read all bytes
  0d0f9a06ab only re-use old connection if valid
  f87323a359 properly fall back on soft seek failure
  bd51105806 infer default s->willclose based on request header
  e5a3c5e409 accept case-insensitive Connection header value
  2dbe4517f6 split request size determination to separate function
  1e1e95f1a2 make reconnection message less misleading
  ee2bc31032 imply keep-alive by default when beneficial
  2ff5405601 reject a Content-Range whose end lies before its start
  332ead500a clear the status code before each request
  17afe2331a drop the old reply when seeking past the end
  5db1e097dc end a read at the end offset with EOF
  ca5300c9f4 end or continue a reply at the end of its range
  faab9c8e56 keep complete size for Content-Range "bytes A-B/*"
  f15077f767 read the whole trailer section of a chunked reply
  b77de7cb6f clear the end of a chunked reply for every request
  8e9ce80c62 check every reply against the requested range
  461f48ece8 stop at the end offset or the end of the file

Left out are the commits to the same file that do something else: the
cookie rules, the response status line parser (which also drops legacy
ICY replies), the protocol checks on redirects, the Cache-Control fix,
the ICY parser's move to http.h and the cosmetic reordering of
HTTPContext (faab9c8e56's three fields are added to the old layout
instead). b77de7cb6f's reset of chunkend in http_connect() is the line
patch 0023 already carries; its other hunk (the break at the end of a
chunked body in http_read_stream()) is still not upstream, so 0023
stays. Drop this patch when the pin moves to a release with all of
these commits: release/9.1 has them, n9.0.2 stops before 2dbe4517f6 and
n8.1.3 earlier.

Without the new options nothing changes on the wire: every request is
open-ended and says "Connection: close", and each seek is a connection.
Patch 0081 fixes what this backport gets wrong on its own; mpv patch
0241 sets the options and has the numbers.

test_http_persistent.sh reads a resource through the patched protocol
from servers that keep connections alive, close them, ignore Range, send
chunked bodies, redirect, cut a reply short, stall, cap a range or do
not know the total size.

